# Copy to infra/.env and adjust for your network. docker compose reads it automatically.
# Everything has a working default — you only need this file for the 3-phone LAN demo.

# Set all three to the laptop's LAN IP for the 3-phone demo (find it with
# `ipconfig` / `ifconfig`). Same IP the app's EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL points at.

# MinIO endpoint presigned report-upload URLs are signed against (phones PUT here).
#S3_ENDPOINT=http://192.168.1.50:9000

# LiveKit (in-app video). LIVEKIT_NODE_IP is the IP the SFU advertises for WebRTC
# media; LIVEKIT_URL is the websocket address handed to the phones. Both = LAN IP.
#LIVEKIT_NODE_IP=192.168.1.50
#LIVEKIT_URL=ws://192.168.1.50:7880

# --- LiveKit Cloud fallback (if LAN media misbehaves; free tier, no card) ---
# Create a project at cloud.livekit.io, then set these to its values and DO NOT
# run the self-hosted `livekit` service. Also set LIVEKIT_API_KEY / _SECRET.
#LIVEKIT_URL=wss://your-project.livekit.cloud
#LIVEKIT_API_KEY=APIxxxxxxxx
#LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=your-cloud-secret
